    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that factory example makes sense. can you expand a bit on the pros and cons of horizontal scaling specifically? like, what are the main challenges when we try to scale out like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When implementing horizontal scaling, pros include:\n\n* Increased capacity to handle larger traffic loads\n* Improved fault tolerance, as multiple servers can continue to function even if one fails\n* Scalability across all instances, reducing the need for manual intervention\n\nHowever, significant challenges arise during horizontal scaling, including:\n\n* Increased complexity and management overhead\n* Higher operational costs due to added servers and maintenance requirements\n* Difficulty in maintaining consistency and data integration across multiple servers\n* Potential issues with session persistence and unified user experience\n\nThese challenges highlight the importance of thorough planning and execution when implementing horizontal scaling.",
      "source": "target",
